#: ../../BaTiO3/lattice-constant.rst:5
msgid "格子定数"
msgstr "Lattice Constants"

#: ../../BaTiO3/lattice-constant.rst:7
msgid ""
"BaTiO₃ の 4 つの結晶相について、各相の対称性を保ちながら\\ `可変セル最適化 <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/electronic/structure_optimization.html#variable-cell-"
"optimization>`__\\ でセルを最適化し、格子定数を求めます。\\ 実験値を基準とした平均相対誤差は、DFT では OpenMX "
"が約 0.34%、QE が約 0.42% でした。\\ 機械学習原子間ポテンシャル（MLIP）では、約 1.4～1.5% でした。\\ MLIP "
"の誤差が最も大きい項目は正方晶の :math:`c/a` で、3.07～3.92% でした（DFT では 0.30～0.31%）。\\ "
"平均を取ったのは 8 項目（立方晶の :math:`a`、正方晶の :math:`a, c/a`、斜方晶の :math:`a, b, "
"c`、菱面体晶の :math:`a, \\alpha`）です。"
msgstr ""
"We determine the lattice constants of the four crystal phases of BaTiO₃ "
"by optimizing each cell with \\  `variable-cell optimization <https"
"://technical-notes.quemix.com/electronic/structure_optimization.html"
"#variable-cell-optimization>`__ \\  while preserving the phase symmetry. "
"\\  The mean relative errors with respect to the experimental values were"
" about 0.34% for OpenMX and about 0.42% for QE in the DFT calculations. "
"\\  For the machine-learning interatomic potentials (MLIPs), the mean "
"errors were about 1.4–1.5%. \\  The largest errors for the MLIPs were in "
"the tetragonal :math:`c/a` ratio, at 3.07–3.92% (0.30–0.31% for DFT). \\"
"  We averaged over 8 quantities: :math:`a` for cubic, :math:`a, c/a` for "
"tetragonal, :math:`a, b, c` for orthorhombic, and :math:`a, \\alpha` for "
"rhombohedral."

#: ../../BaTiO3/lattice-constant.rst:13
msgid ""
"計算値は 0 K の最適化構造、実験値は各相が安定な温度域で測定した値です。\\ "
"両者の差には、交換相関汎関数の近似によるずれに加えて、熱膨張などの温度の影響も含まれます（技術ノートの\\ `LDAとGGA（PBE） "
"<https://technical-notes.quemix.com/electronic/exchange_correlation.html"
"#exchange-correlation-functional>`__\\ と\\ `熱膨張と準調和近似 <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/phonon_thermal.html#thermal-expansion>`__）。"
msgstr ""
"The calculated values are for structures optimized at 0 K, whereas the "
"experimental values were measured in the temperature range where each "
"phase is stable. \\  The differences include temperature effects such as "
"thermal expansion as well as deviations due to the approximate exchange-"
"correlation functional (see the Technical Notes sections on \\  `LDA and "
"GGA (PBE) <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/electronic/exchange_correlation.html#exchange-"
"correlation-functional>`__ \\  and \\  `thermal expansion and the quasi-"
"harmonic approximation <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/phonon_thermal.html#thermal-expansion>`__)."

#: ../../BaTiO3/lattice-constant.rst:164
msgid "格子最適化に用いた入力ファイル例"
msgstr "Example Input Files for Lattice Optimization"

#: ../../BaTiO3/lattice-constant.rst:166
msgid ""
"Quloud で計算するには、下のブロックから対象の手法・相の入力例を開きます。\\ "
"コピーした内容で、ジョブの対応する入力ファイルを置き換えます。\\ 使用するファイルは OpenMX では ``openmx.in``、QE では"
" ``QuloudJob.scf.in``、ASE では ``ase.in``、LAMMPS では ``in.QuloudJob`` です。"
msgstr ""
"To run a calculation in Quloud, open the example input for the method and"
" phase of interest below. \\  Copy its contents and use them to replace "
"the corresponding input file in the Job. \\  The files are ``openmx.in`` "
"for OpenMX, ``QuloudJob.scf.in`` for QE, ``ase.in`` for ASE, and "
"``in.QuloudJob`` for LAMMPS."

#: ../../BaTiO3/lattice-constant.rst:170
msgid ""
"格子だけを比べるため、内部座標を固定し、相ごとに許される格子の自由度だけを動かしました（下の表「相ごとのセル拘束」）。\\ "
"晶系ごとに保つ関係と、分率座標を固定してセルを変える計算の意味は、技術ノートの\\ `対称性を保つ格子と原子座標の拘束 <https"
"://technical-notes.quemix.com/electronic/structure_optimization.html"
"#symmetry-constrained-relaxation>`__\\ にまとめました。"
msgstr ""
"To compare the lattices alone, we fixed the internal coordinates and "
"varied only the lattice degrees of freedom allowed for each phase (see "
"the table “Cell constraints by phase” below). \\  The Technical Notes "
"section on \\  `symmetry-preserving constraints on the lattice and atomic"
" coordinates <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/electronic/structure_optimization.html#symmetry-"
"constrained-relaxation>`__ \\  explains the geometric relations preserved"
" in each crystal system and what it means to vary the cell while keeping "
"fractional coordinates fixed."

#: ../../BaTiO3/lattice-constant.rst:173
msgid ""
"そのため、OpenMXでは相に応じて ``OptC3``、``OptC4``、``OptC2`` "
"を使い分けました。これは、最適化の途中で立方晶、正方晶、斜方晶、菱面体晶の特徴が混ざったり、別の相へ崩れたりすることを避けるためです。QEでは同じ考え方を"
" ``vc-relax`` と ``cell_dofree = 'ibrav'`` "
"により実装しました。MLIPのASE/LAMMPS入力は、同じ構造ファイルに対してセルを含む緩和を行うための例として示しました。"
msgstr ""
"For that purpose, we used ``OptC3``, ``OptC4``, or ``OptC2`` in OpenMX, "
"depending on the phase. The purpose is to keep the optimization from "
"mixing the characteristics of the cubic, tetragonal, orthorhombic, and "
"rhombohedral phases or allowing relaxation into another phase. In QE, we "
"imposed analogous constraints with ``vc-relax`` and ``cell_dofree = "
"'ibrav'``. The MLIP inputs for ASE and LAMMPS illustrate relaxation that "
"includes the cell for the same structure files."

#: ../../BaTiO3/lattice-constant.rst:175
